  "term": "vocalization",
  "definition": "Vocalization is the production of voiced sounds, such as in singing or toning. In this context, toning is a vocalization practice in which a person sustains a sound during exhalation, and such practices have been linked with relaxation, emotion regulation, and social closeness.",
